{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855779Z","id":"d00b8522e108554edd0dbdc2179840a7a8bee0f5ab73d0f2c6417287c6e91721","body":{"detail":"Per-agent narrowing and raising act on one session, but every agent of a connected machine signs with the same grant credential, so a narrowed agent's sibling on the same machine can act for it. People builds the per-agent controls and shows MACHINE_BOUNDARY beside them (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte, both the narrow and raise panels). If each agent session gets its own credential, this line changes or goes; it is the one constant to edit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"b9c10a0fd1241155948d899c77303e56757cd101af254488c493bde172ab337d"},"summary":"The machine-boundary line stands for per-agent controls that sibling sessions can bypass","tags":["revisit:per-session agent credentials are decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855849Z","id":"d3a77187ab40c8951702a77e1abda27f00151bdb12ac792b53b4970bfc03cb73","body":{"detail":"machineCaps/agentCaps treat a capability as on when any access object of its type grants the action anywhere, and narrowGrant/narrowAgent build a narrowing as the person's rights less whole actions. A narrowing made outside People (location-limited, from a script) shows as fully on for an action it grants at one artifact, and an agent narrowing built on such a machine narrowing can be refused 400 not_narrower (shown as the daemon words it). No route makes location-limited narrowings today besides direct API calls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"94fa9f9f7aaec826bea13c4880fbd5d2110d4970ca56dd0c16c9d2303deba841"},"summary":"People reads and builds narrowings by whole actions, ignoring locations","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855887Z","id":"9b37d8dce5820c899da52cf299a93663649f27a8c6418a23c977dea3bd3d52e6","body":{"detail":"Spec section 3.4's example raises an agent for one artifact (Publish versions of \"Quarterly Review\"). People raises an action at \"*\" only, which keeps the panel to one list of checkboxes; the route takes locations, so a per-artifact raise is a UI addition.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"6149476116b6fdf827b3dd235aa856cc5f10de23b97a42e122f6bb285bb4a081"},"summary":"Raises are at every artifact; no per-artifact raise in People","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to raise an agent for one artifact","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855925Z","id":"9f714fe521f4d7eee66fedcdaa059787db5f51c66dc0793d781eee871752db93","body":{"detail":"Spec section 17 lists approvals in both directions on the owner's People. The card shows the owner's approvals of the person's content (GET /api/approvals is the caller's own) and what waits on the owner; whether the person lets the owner's content reach their agents is not readable by the owner: GET /api/people carries no approvals and GET /api/approvals is scoped to the caller's person. Needs a server read before the UI can show it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"7dbb794ed83617037dbc89745d86b4ef640ea8c19cf2fc7c1e312f5ae41b588d"},"summary":"The owner sees approvals in one direction only","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/InviteDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855953Z","id":"534d258c6a99631ed7bf6f45245ba08b45abe8e0d7b5a64cd970d871bae90729","body":{"detail":"POST /api/people/invites takes {viewer} (spec section 6.2), but the dialog offers only a new person or the owner's own machine. Naming a new person after a viewer who was never invited is 409 name_taken, whose message says to invite that viewer, which People cannot do yet. A viewer picker would use GET /api/viewers?q=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"5aed600e45e79d959736f2f8b5fad319e35a36576ba1a9b733b99cfe892345cf"},"summary":"No invite for an existing LAN viewer","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.855989Z","id":"cbce4d8bdb806b2f9030e911c2cd2a2e229ac4d454ea05a30509bf050475698c","body":{"detail":"People lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228575Z","id":"2a0f0513adaefb7d58fac0a83843b3943f421eb1b1b53beef2ca5eb35dfd3f3c","body":{"detail":"PeopleApproval carries artifact_id and thread_id but no title; the owner's card and the person's 'Who reaches your agents' (web/shell/src/people/People.svelte:141-143) show only the scope, so two thread approvals of one author cannot be told apart before revoking one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"3957ae22c46a99406d445359da28bbf765a8e7b4a9992fd5b6b0888f42752cc2"},"suggested_fix":"Name the artifact (its title, linked to the thread) beside the scope: add the title to approval_view in crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs, filtered as the approver's browser may read it, or look it up from the gallery's artifact list.","summary":"Approval rows say 'Allowed on one page' or 'Allowed in one thread' without naming the page or the thread","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228632Z","id":"974ad66dea4143a306e1a8ded94a7a00d0e99b49990cf877afaa9b9d302a656d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9f714fe521f4d7eee66fedcdaa059787db5f51c66dc0793d781eee871752db93","summary":"A spec gap, not only a missing read: section 17 promises approvals in both directions, but section 7.5 makes GET /api/approvals Own, section 9.5 lists one direction for People, and no route gives the owner a person's approvals. The owner decides whether the owner may read them (and whether only of the owner's content or of every author), then section 17 or section 7.5 is amended to match.","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228669Z","id":"8abe4c3ed7ce6b03c0fabd1364de80b2445cfb4490f04f18f63ce1ba9dd675b3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9b37d8dce5820c899da52cf299a93663649f27a8c6418a23c977dea3bd3d52e6","summary":"Beyond the location: raiseCaps (model.ts:113-116) counts an action as held when the person's rights grant it anywhere, so for a Collaborator 'Publish new versions' and 'Delete artifacts' (granted on own only) show checked and disabled, and People cannot raise them at all. Section 3.4's example (Publish versions of one artifact for a Collaborator's agent) is impossible in the UI, not only narrower. A Collaborator holds every one of the 13 actions somewhere, so for an agent of the default preset every raise checkbox is checked and disabled and People can raise nothing; in a browser, only the actions the person had narrowed off were enabled.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228737Z","id":"a70a305cc7475e614211ec5fdcc67505eb821629c034ea3696939101504e06f6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d00b8522e108554edd0dbdc2179840a7a8bee0f5ab73d0f2c6417287c6e91721","summary":"Per-agent credentials were chosen on 2026-10-12. When each agent session signs with its own credential, MACHINE_BOUNDARY (model.ts:10) and its two uses in web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte (lines 132 and 142) change in the same change.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.883856Z","id":"f43f2d8b5e1786aae2b40708c4796febcbf3cc58f997eb520390bb543cbe512f","body":{"detail":"machineCaps/agentCaps treat a capability as on when any access object of its type grants the action anywhere, and narrowGrant/narrowAgent build a narrowing as the person's rights less whole actions. A narrowing made outside People (location-limited, from a script) shows as fully on for an action it grants at one artifact, and an agent narrowing built on such a machine narrowing can be refused 400 not_narrower (shown as the daemon words it). No route makes location-limited narrowings today besides direct API calls. Raises (raiseCaps, elevation) are by location: an action is held only where the unraised rights allow it there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"485a6bbee1728e95fd9064cc6fa033b878dea45f964a111edd092836c2bece8a"},"summary":"People reads and builds narrowings by whole actions, ignoring locations","supersedes":"d3a77187ab40c8951702a77e1abda27f00151bdb12ac792b53b4970bfc03cb73","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.884633Z","id":"1b80cc4d5ab2c276004f0603af7967360282105d186ad37cc3da1cc93ebda9f3","body":{"detail":"Spec section 17 lists approvals in both directions on the owner's People. The card shows the owner's approvals of the person's content (GET /api/approvals is the caller's own) and what waits on the owner; whether the person lets the owner's content reach their agents is not readable by the owner: GET /api/people carries no approvals and GET /api/approvals is scoped to the caller's person. Needs a server read before the UI can show it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"3ec70c8b6f05ea8b20aa108074b8b7f57b5d586ce3b9046a683aafbbe06883e3"},"summary":"The owner sees approvals in one direction only","supersedes":"9f714fe521f4d7eee66fedcdaa059787db5f51c66dc0793d781eee871752db93","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/InviteDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.885341Z","id":"1001bc9803945a25411738180887d1ebdab3e23dd9057317de5ddffe31c39725","body":{"detail":"POST /api/people/invites takes {viewer} (spec section 6.2), but the dialog offers only a new person or the owner's own machine. Naming a new person after a viewer who was never invited is 409 name_taken, whose message says to invite that viewer, which People cannot do yet. A viewer picker would use GET /api/viewers?q=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":67},"content_hash":"5aed600e45e79d959736f2f8b5fad319e35a36576ba1a9b733b99cfe892345cf"},"summary":"No invite for an existing LAN viewer","supersedes":"534d258c6a99631ed7bf6f45245ba08b45abe8e0d7b5a64cd970d871bae90729","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.886060Z","id":"4f66d956d05b45ed610223f45109389a3cc64d029db8a13fd4c0037722835290","body":{"detail":"People lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"cbce4d8bdb806b2f9030e911c2cd2a2e229ac4d454ea05a30509bf050475698c","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.886686Z","id":"d9c7672405a3113bea7e8664d0b72679c446253cbd106d534da3e9da67f5156a","body":{"detail":"raiseCaps tests the unraised rights at the artifact's ID, and an `own` location never covers a bare artifact ID (narrowerOrEqual's within). People does not know which artifacts are the person's (the artifact list carries no creator person), so for a Collaborator's agent 'Publish new versions' and 'Delete artifacts' at one of the person's own artifacts show unchecked and raisable. Raising there adds nothing the agent lacked; it only says less than it could. Fixing it needs the artifacts' person in GET /api/artifacts or a per-artifact rights check route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"2920b50211feb7bfd4fc12cf7f96d2345f50abb8a6b0e84b4167a6d1e2dc53df"},"summary":"A raise at one of the person's own artifacts shows as not held","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.887393Z","id":"78560dd6d7f4509d046ad133a6563e378d0cd0797bcbb7d12d9b567a2171b6af","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e346be1d","summary":"Approval views carry artifact_title (8b8a8051), and approval rows say 'Allowed on “<title>”' or 'Allowed in one thread on “<title>”' (e346be1d). Evidence: PersonCard.test.ts 'names an approval's page when the daemon names it' passes; integration test approvals_name_the_owner_as_such_and_their_page asserts artifact_title 'Quarterly Review'.","supersedes":"2a0f0513adaefb7d58fac0a83843b3943f421eb1b1b53beef2ca5eb35dfd3f3c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.888050Z","id":"1bb5828a4bdd86518362febb7c60c363a91960b192a373af2754852ec51733b7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e346be1d","summary":"People's raise panel now takes a place, every artifact or one artifact from the live list, and counts an action as held only where the unraised rights allow it there. Evidence: model.test.ts 'counts an action as held only where the agent's rights allow it, so a Collaborator's agent can be raised to publish versions' and PersonCard.test.ts 'raises a Collaborator's agent to publish versions of one artifact' pass; e2e/people.spec.ts raises Sam's agent at one artifact and reads elevate [{type: clax-artifacts, actions: [update], locations: [<id>]}] from GET /api/people.","supersedes":"9b37d8dce5820c899da52cf299a93663649f27a8c6418a23c977dea3bd3d52e6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.166253Z","id":"b714cf82b695aa82d6ba568c91acfba8af3a5186a181207c3f81361488bb95bd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9cfb85d5","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"399219efcda16cc7dbd6bca66609f58287688c0ce278c5e4134220f124177d6e"},"summary":"The inbox's connection card approves a request with its code, a new person's name and a preset (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Evidence: npx vitest run shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.test.ts passes ('enables Approve only with a typed code and a name for the new person, and approves with both and the preset'), and npx playwright test e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts passes, Kim's clax connect finishing after the owner approves in the inbox.","supersedes":"4f66d956d05b45ed610223f45109389a3cc64d029db8a13fd4c0037722835290","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741455Z","id":"5d149ae5227939920d701dd126c632ad885b6717ecdb226f2917daf667553180","body":{"detail":"Failure: a request whose comment has 3 lines of about 145 characters each (or 1-3 lines that together wrap past 3 visual lines, each under 160 characters). `long` (line 56) is false, since there are not more than 3 logical lines and none is over 160 characters, so no Show all button renders, while `.acard .held:not([data-open]) .htext` (line 120) clamps to 3 visual lines. Measured in Chromium on a scratch daemon: the card's .htext had scrollHeight > clientHeight with no .show button at both 1280 and 390 px; line 2 ended in an ellipsis and line 3 was invisible, before and after deciding. The approver decides without being able to read the withheld content (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md §9.5, §26 (d)). No test covers it: deleting the 160-character clause leaves web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.test.ts passing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"8750c5fa6f86baf5eb6681800c5e9c7b4f459c1ffd0bf16a2b2778e5c336c5ec"},"suggested_fix":"Decide Show all from the rendered box (scrollHeight > clientHeight after layout, rechecked on resize), or clamp by logical lines only and let each shown line wrap in full; add a test with three long lines.","summary":"Withheld content is clipped with no Show all when its first lines wrap: the 3-line CSS clamp hides text that `long` does not count","tags":["review","task:21","severity:important","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
